# CYS-CAA — Cys-S to α-chloroacetamide post-substitution adduct
#
# Hand-authored link CIF for PyKeko covalent-ligand workflow.
# Family F3 of the plan-doc taxonomy: covers chloroacetamide-warhead
# drugs and tool compounds where Cys-S displaces Cl via SN2 on the
# α-carbon of an acetamide. Examples: many GSK probes, PROTAC linkers,
# clinical KRAS-G12C series (though those use the related fluoromethyl
# /acrylamide variants).
#
# Mechanism:
#   R-N-C(=O)-CH₂-Cl  +  Cys-S⁻  →  R-N-C(=O)-CH₂-S-Cys  +  Cl⁻
#                          (SN2 displacement of chloride)
#
# Geometric difference vs F1/F2: only ONE carbon is in play (the α-
# methylene that takes the SG). There is no "Cβ" past it — the
# placeholder convention reuses <CB> for the attack carbon for
# consistency with the detector's output, and skips <CA>/<CG>/<HCA>
# which have no analogue in this chemistry.
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <LIG> ← ligand 3-letter (or 5-char) CCD code
#   <CB>  ← attack-site C atom-id (the α-methylene C in -C(=O)-CH₂-Cl)
#   <CO>  ← carbonyl-C atom-id (sp2, bound to =O and N)
#   <N>   ← amide-N atom-id
#   <O>   ← carbonyl-O atom-id
#   <CL>  ← leaving Cl atom-id (pre-reaction input only)
#   <HCB> ← H to delete on Cβ (post-product input only)
#
# Geometry provenance:
#   * S-C(sp3 methylene): CSD aggregate 1.81 ± 0.02 Å — same value as
#     F1 acrylamide post-product (both are sp3 thioether linkages)
#   * CB-S-C: 100° ± 3° (Cys side, sp3 sulfur to sp3 carbon)
#   * S-C-C(=O): 110° ± 2° (sp3 tetrahedral C with one carbonyl
#     neighbour — narrower than the pure tetrahedral 109.5° because
#     the carbonyl draws electron density off the α-carbon)
#   * No planarity restraint — sp3/sp3 system has rotational freedom
#
# Differences from F1 CYS-ACR.cif:
#   * No SG-Cβ-Cγ angle (Cβ has no Cγ; instead its other heavy
#     neighbour is the carbonyl-C, handled by SG-Cβ-CO)
#   * No sp3-sp3 thioether torsion (only one C-C bond past Cβ exists,
#     the Cβ-CO bond, and that's a sp3-sp2 hinge handled below)
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf — CCP4-ML link-CIF format
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md §2.3 (F3 chloroacetamide family)

data_link_CYS-CAA
_chem_link.id                CYS-CAA
_chem_link.name              "Cys-S to alpha-chloroacetamide post-substitution adduct"
_chem_link.comp_id_1         CYS
_chem_link.mod_id_1          CYS-CAA-mod1
_chem_link.group_comp_1      L-peptide
_chem_link.comp_id_2         <LIG>
_chem_link.mod_id_2          CYS-CAA-mod2
_chem_link.group_comp_2      non-polymer

# ---- bonds: new S-Cβ single bond (sp3 S to sp3 C) ----
loop_
_chem_link_bond.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_link_bond.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_link_bond.type
_chem_link_bond.value_dist
_chem_link_bond.value_dist_esd
 1 SG    2 <CB>   single 1.81 0.02

# ---- angles around the new sp3 thioether linkage ----
# Cys side: same range as F1 sp3 thioether.
# Ligand side: SG-Cβ-CO ~110° (sp3 C with one carbonyl neighbour pulling
# the angle slightly inward from ideal tetrahedral).
loop_
_chem_link_angle.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_1
_chem_link_angle.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_2
_chem_link_angle.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_3
_chem_link_angle.value_angle
_chem_link_angle.value_angle_esd
 1 CB    1 SG    2 <CB>   100.0   3.0
 1 SG    2 <CB>  2 <CO>   110.0   2.0

# ---- soft torsion on the sp3-sp2 hinge ----
# The Cβ-CO bond is the only post-bond rotatable axis. Period=3 lets the
# carbonyl rotate to relieve any clashes the Cys orientation imposes;
# σ=20° keeps it gentle.
loop_
_chem_link_tor.id
_chem_link_tor.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_1
_chem_link_tor.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_2
_chem_link_tor.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_3
_chem_link_tor.atom_4_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_4
_chem_link_tor.value_angle
_chem_link_tor.value_angle_esd
_chem_link_tor.period
 sp3_sp2_hinge 1 SG    2 <CB>  2 <CO>  2 <N>    180.0  20.0  3


# =====================================================================
# Cys-side modification: delete HG (the thiol H) — identical to F1/F2 mod1
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-CAA-mod1
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-CAA-mod1 delete HG . . . .


# =====================================================================
# Ligand-side modification — POST-PRODUCT SATURATED INPUT BRANCH.
#
# User uploaded a ligand where the α-methylene C has already had Cl
# replaced with -S-Cys, so the ligand carries a spare H on Cβ that's
# replaced by the new SG bond. Just delete that H.
#
# If the runtime detector instead matched the chloride pre-reaction
# form (free drug SMILES, R-N-C(=O)-CH₂-Cl), use CYS-CAA-mod2-chloride.cif
# which deletes Cl + the Cβ-Cl bond rather than an H.
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-CAA-mod2
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-CAA-mod2 delete <HCB> . . . .
